From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/50] ASoC: sm8150: accept the DisplayPort back end

A DisplayPort back end reaches the machine driver with a DAI id (104,
DISPLAY_PORT_RX) that none of its three switches list, so opening, configuring
and closing a stream to an external display each log an "invalid dai id" error.
The streams are not rejected - those default branches only print - but the log
is misleading.

The DisplayPort controller configures its own audio path, so there is nothing
for the machine driver to do beyond not complaining.

Source: hotdog-linux-bringup
aports/device/testing/linux-oneplus-hotdog-mainline616/0051-asoc-sm8150-accept-the-displayport-backend.patch
(https://github.com/Sr-0w/hotdog-linux-bringup); rebased onto this tree, where
0008 already moved QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX into its own shutdown case.

Signed-off-by: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Nura-Category: reference-port
Nura-Origin: hotdog-linux-bringup 0051
Upstream-Status: n/a: sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c is fork-only
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
index 93294d6..459f7ea 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
@@ -209,6 +209,9 @@ static int sm8150_snd_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	case SLIMBUS_0_RX...SLIMBUS_6_TX:
 		ret = sm8150_slim_snd_hw_params(substream, params);
 		break;
+	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX:
+		/* the DP controller configures its own audio path */
+		break;
 	default:
 		pr_err("%s: invalid dai id 0x%x\n", __func__, cpu_dai->id);
 		break;
@@ -335,6 +338,7 @@ static int sm8150_snd_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(codec_dai, codec_dai_fmt);
 		break;
 	case SLIMBUS_0_RX...SLIMBUS_6_TX:
+	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX:
 		break;
 	default:
 		pr_err("%s: invalid dai id 0x%x\n", __func__, cpu_dai->id);
@@ -366,6 +370,8 @@ static void sm8150_snd_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 			Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_QUAD_MI2S_IBIT,
 			0, SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK);
 		break;
+	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX:
+		break;
 	default:
 		pr_err("%s: invalid dai id 0x%x\n", __func__, cpu_dai->id);
 		break;
